WEBVTT

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.210
Friendship

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:22.370
thief

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:22.370
parent and child crooks

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:31.090
<b>Episode 8: It's a Game Where You Wait, and Wait, and Wait... and Keep Waiting</b>

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:35.280
<b>Episode 8: It's a Game Where You Wait, and Wait, and Wait... and Keep Waiting</b>

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:38.130
We still have some time. 
We've got to find a perfect hiding spot.

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.320
You're right.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:43.560
Especially because this game 
has such specific rules.

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:48.000
<b>Before the start of the third game</b>

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:48.040
All right then, 
I'll explain each of the rules.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.830
Drumroll...

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:50.840
Ta-da!

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.750
Things You Can't Do

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.750
Violence

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.750
Moving the Hider

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.750
Things You Can Do

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.750
Contact

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.750
Food

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.750
Surrender (Give Up)

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.750
Change Sides (Switch)

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:53.750
Let's start with the things 
you simply cannot do.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.380
<b>Things You Can't Do</b>

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.380
<b>Violence</b>

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:56.380
One: Violence.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:58.510
Tell us where!

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:59.010
You can't use violence 
against the other team

00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:02.890
Where is he?!

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:03.030
to force them to give up 
the hider's location. That's forbidden.

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:05.270
<b>No Good</b>

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:05.660
That should be obvious.

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:08.520
<b>Things You Can't Do</b>

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:08.520
<b>Moving the Hider</b>

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:08.510
Two: Moving the hider.

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:12.590
Once the hider has settled on a spot, 
they are forbidden from moving.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.650
Are they coming? Are they coming?

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:16.080
You can't leave that spot 
until the game is over.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:17.030
<b>No Good</b>

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:21.630
It's really harsh that we can't 
move after choosing a hiding spot.

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:22.910
Yeah.

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:25.800
There are surveillance 
cameras all over the place.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:27.710
If you move even a little...

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:32.240
If you do something you're not 
allowed to, there's a penalty.

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:36.980
Your team's debts will all double, 
and you will instantly lose.

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:38.510
So be careful!

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:42.060
I'd hoped we'd be able to 
investigate Tomodachi Game a bit

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:45.510
now that we made it all the way 
to the third round.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:47.670
This game might make that difficult.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:51.730
Especially since this is the only way 
we can contact each other.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:51.730
<b></b>Swipe screen to unlock

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:54.860
Next, the things you <i>can</i> do.

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:59.240
I'll give each of you one cell phone.

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:01.860
<b>Things You Can Do</b>

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:01.860
<b>Contact</b>

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:01.860
One: Contact.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:06.370
Every player of this game can 
contact anyone else, friend or foe,

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:06.370
This is annoying.

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:10.330
so if you get into trouble, 
call for help, okay?

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:13.440
He said we can call anytime,

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:19.350
but unless there's a serious emergency, 
I don't think you'll hear from me.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:22.480
Tenji!

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:25.600
What's wrong? Are you okay?

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.970
Y-Yeah. Just a little dizzy.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:33.060
I'm not surprised. We haven't 
eaten in three days.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:37.820
Damn it. They could have let us eat 
something before the game started.

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:40.320
<b>Things You Can Do</b>

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:40.320
<b>Food</b>

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:40.320
Two: Food.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.070
We eatin'

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:45.060
Right in the middle of the forest, 
there's a stash of food ready for you.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:49.410
Once the game starts, you can eat 
as much and as often as you want.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:54.870
Huh, Group C hasn't eaten anything yet.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:04:01.230
Oh, and the searchers have to 
bring food to the hiders.

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:04.300
Remember, the hiders aren't allowed to move!

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:09.320
Sorry. I'm better now.

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:12.160
Are you sure? Maybe you should rest more.

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:13.290
No, it's okay.

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:16.940
If I let something like this slow me down, 
we'll never beat this thing.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:20.570
Things You Can't Do

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:20.570
Violence

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:20.570
Moving the Hider

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:20.570
Things You Can Do

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:20.570
Contact

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:20.570
Food

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:20.570
Surrender (Give Up)

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:20.570
Change Sides (Switch)

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:20.920
The next one is a right 
that is given only to the hider.

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:23.320
<b>Things You Can Do</b>

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:23.320
<b>Surrender (Give Up)</b>

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:23.540
That's three: Give up.

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:27.830
I'm so bored

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:30.450
I'm so lonely

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:33.750
<b>Hider</b>

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:27.680
This game is actually harder for the hiders.

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:30.300
Well, yeah, they're stuck alone and bored.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:33.750
Sittin' still for a long time 
kinda wears you out.

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:36.320
Yeah. So in case you're waiting forever,

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:40.140
but your searcher can't find 
the other team's hider,

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:42.090
and you can't take it anymore,

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:44.510
you have a give-up button!

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:49.470
It's just what it sounds like. Press this, 
and your group will immediately lose.

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:53.770
It's not your fault if your teammates
 are cruel and incompetent.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:58.420
By the way, it only counts 
if the owner presses it.

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:02.150
<b>Things You Can Do</b>

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:02.150
<b>Change Sides (Switch)</b>

00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:02.150
Finally, the fourth one is changing sides.

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:03.610
Let me join you!

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:03.610
Come on over!

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:03.610
Come on over!

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:04.700
I already explained that, so we're good.

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:09.080
All right, each team, 
please choose your hiders.

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:14.330
I'm not worried about you, Yuichi, 
but that girl could be trouble.

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:17.040
She's a total stranger.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:20.540
<b>Drop Out</b>

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:20.540
There's a good chance she could choose 
to lose and drop out by herself.

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:25.010
Well, that's on her. I bet she 
feels helpless alone, though.

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:33.270
All right, nobody should find you here. 
Especially with that pit in the back.

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:34.500
Where's the girl?

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.210
Don't worry.

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:39.350
Just to be safe, 
I left her waiting far away.

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:41.360
She won't know where this is.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:45.240
Yuichi, remember what you said?

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:49.800
But it would be almost impossible 
for the two of us to win.

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:52.640
Can we win with three?

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:55.450
The other team will still have twice 
as many people searching for me.

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:59.330
Even with three, if we play clean, 
it's probably impossible.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:04.220
So basically, if we don't play clean, 
we might be able to pull it off?

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:11.250
If we don't play clean, it'll all 
depend on how much you can handle.

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:12.180
Probably.

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:18.190
No matter what I do, you've got to 
hold on, hold on, and keep holding on...

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:21.080
As long as you don't push 
the give-up button,

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.560
we definitely have a chance to win.

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:27.320
Don't worry, Yuichi. I won't 
give up, no matter what.

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:28.950
Tenji...

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:36.660
Like I said, you're the last hope 
I have to avenge my father.

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:41.500
I'll do anything to regain your trust.

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:45.750
All right. That's a relief, then.

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:47.840
I'm sure we can win!

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:51.010
Okay, it's almost been two hours.

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:55.410
I didn't really get a chance 
to explain my plan,

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:58.110
but it's too risky to stay
 here, so I'd better go.

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:00.280
Got it. I'm counting on you.

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:02.990
I'll finish and come back as soon as I can,

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:06.110
so just trust me and wait, Tenji.

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:10.100
Yeah, I'll trust you and be waiting, Yuichi.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:13.380
<i>But after that...</i>

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:19.330
<i>Yuichi didn't come back for two full days.</i>

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:27.960
<i>Why hasn't Yuichi come back yet?</i>

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:32.510
<i>Is it that hard to find 
someone in this huge forest?</i>

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:36.800
<i>There's no sign of the other 
team looking for me, either.</i>

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:40.550
<i>We might be in for a really long fight.</i>

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:42.830
<i>But even so...</i>

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:49.080
<i>Even so, couldn't he just 
bring me some food and water?</i>

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:51.520
<i>Wouldn't that be okay?</i>

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:58.660
<i>Or maybe... has Yuichi betrayed me?!</i>

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:05.290
<i>If that's the case, maybe 
he already switched teams</i>

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:07.900
<i>and is leading them here now...</i>

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:12.220
<i>No, that still wouldn't take this much time.</i>

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:16.220
<i>Why, then? Why hasn't Yuichi come back?</i>

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:19.340
<i>It's starting to feel 
like I'm being abused—</i>

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:23.980
<i>Wait, abused? Is Yuichi trying to abuse me?</i>

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:28.040
<i>I totally betrayed everyone 
in the second game,</i>

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:31.240
<i>but then when he called a truce, 
I let my guard down...</i>

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:37.150
<i>He's been waiting for a chance 
to get revenge in the third game!</i>

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:43.360
<i>Right now, Yuichi's probably relaxing 
and eating with that girl,</i>

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:48.840
<b>Ahahaha!</b>

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:47.620
<i>laughing at me while he imagines 
me suffering! Isn't he?</i>

00:08:56.620 --> 00:08:58.570
<i>No, I've got to calm down!</i>

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:03.550
<i>I'm so hungry, I can't even think straight.</i>

00:09:06.490 --> 00:09:09.110
<i>That's right! I still have this!</i>

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:13.400
<i>I thought about calling 
after one day had passed,</i>

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.610
<b>Contacts</b>

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.610
<b>Search</b>

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.610
<b></b>Mikasa Tenji (Group C)

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.610
<b></b>Ka

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.610
<b></b>Katagiri Yuichi (Group C)

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.610
<b></b>Kadokura Juzo (Group K)

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.610
<b></b>Sa

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.610
<b></b>Shinomiya Kei (Group K)

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.610
<b></b>Ta

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.610
<b></b>Na

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.610
<b></b>Niwa Banri (Group K)

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.610
<b></b>Ha

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.610
<b></b>Hashiratani Chisato (Group K)

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:18.650
<i>but I held off because I didn't want it 
to look like I doubted Yuichi.</i>

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:22.240
<i>And now I've been waiting two full days.</i>

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:25.620
<i>Maybe if I called saying I was worried 
something happened to him,</i>

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:28.250
<i>it wouldn't sound strange.</i>

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:40.390
<i>Why aren't you answering?!</i>

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:42.350
<i>Yuichi! Yuichi!</i>

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:45.580
<i>Shit, I'm so thirsty! I'm so hungry!</i>

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:47.890
<i>Shit! Shit! Shit!</i>

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:49.770
<b>Incoming call</b>

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:49.770
<b>Katagiri Yuichi (Group C)</b>

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:54.650
Hello, Yuichi?

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:57.660
You didn't come back, 
so I was starting to worry.

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:58.440
How are things over—

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:02.300
<i>Uh, sorry, this is a member of Group K.</i>

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:06.650
What? What do you want?

00:10:06.650 --> 00:10:10.130
<i>Um, this is a little hard to say,</i>

00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:15.070
<i>but Katagiri Yuichi-san 
is planning to abandon you.</i>

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:20.590
There's no way he'd do that.

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:24.410
I know he's searching like crazy 
for your hider right now.

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:29.520
<i>I hate to break it to you, but he 
hasn't gone out searching even once.</i>

00:10:30.220 --> 00:10:34.650
<i>He's just been relaxing with
 that girl, eating and sleeping.</i>

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:38.640
<i>Yuichi-san said,</i>

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:42.840
<i>"Mikasa Tenji totally screwed us 
over in the second game,"</i>

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:45.910
<i>"and I'll absolutely never forgive him."</i>

00:10:47.090 --> 00:10:49.460
<i>If you don't believe me, 
I'll pass him the phone</i>

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:51.000
<i>and you can ask him yourself.</i>

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:52.850
<i>He's right here with me.</i>

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:54.610
<i>I can talk to Yuichi?</i>

00:10:57.630 --> 00:10:59.560
That isn't necessary.

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:03.320
If he needs to, I know Yuichi 
will contact me directly.

00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:06.600
I'll always trust him. 
I'm going to keep waiting.

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:08.700
<i>Is that so?</i>

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:11.400
<i>Well, when you've really had enough,</i>

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:14.270
<i>please be sure to press the give-up button.</i>

00:11:14.590 --> 00:11:16.240
<i>Otherwise, you'll die.</i>

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:44.850
<i>Hurry... Hurry up and come back, Yuichi!</i>

00:11:47.490 --> 00:11:51.030
How is he? What kind of 
shape is their hider in?

00:11:51.030 --> 00:11:55.700
Well, I can tell he's trying to bluff, 
but he sounds like a mess.

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:58.780
He hasn't eaten for a total 
of five days, right?

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:00.270
That would be rough.

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:05.820
And while he's holding his breath 
and hiding from us,

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:08.790
he's gotta keep believing in his friend.

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:12.280
That's gotta be totally 
screwing with his head.

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:17.710
Poor thing. No matter how hard 
he tries, it's pointless.

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:27.220
Because our guy came up 
with a perfect strategy.

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:30.970
<b>Right after the start of the third game</b>

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:34.640
I have a strategy to win 
this Friendly Hide-and-Seek.

00:12:34.950 --> 00:12:37.020
S-Seriously, Captain?

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:39.540
Yeah. We'll definitely win.

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:41.530
<b>Kadokura Juzo</b>

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:41.530
<b>Captain and psychological pillar of Group K. 
Commands absolute trust from his friends.</b>

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:46.280
I knew you would, Captain! 
We'll never go wrong if we listen to you!

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:48.150
<b>Chief of cut-ins in Group K. 
Ready to fight anyone for his friends. 
A hot-blooded virgin punk.</b>

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:48.160
<b>Onigawara Hyakutaro</b>

00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:52.100
You're always trying to flatter the 
captain like that, Hyakutaro.

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:54.410
At least listen to his plan first.

00:12:54.410 --> 00:12:55.920
You shut your face!

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:57.920
<b>Hashiratani Chisato</b>

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:57.920
<b>Group K's lead hottie.
 Smooth with the ladies. 
A pretentious flirt.</b>

00:12:57.930 --> 00:13:04.170
Well, Senpai, the captain's instructions 
have helped us clear everything so far.

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:06.050
<b>Shinomiya Kei</b>

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:06.050
<b>The youngest Group K member. 
A little nervous around his senpai, 
but he always does his best.</b>

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:08.340
Isn't that right, Banri-senpai?

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:10.680
No problem. Everything's fine.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:12.560
<b>Niwa Banri</b>

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:12.560
<b>Group K's geek. 
Hard to read because he's usually
 pretty quiet, but it's best that way!</b>

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:15.050
So, what's the strategy?

00:13:15.050 --> 00:13:19.450
It should become obvious when you think 
about the essence of the game.

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:20.570
Essence?

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:24.990
To begin with, this hide-and-seek game 
isn't about luck or probability.

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:27.660
Kadokura Juzo

00:13:25.550 --> 00:13:27.660
This is still part of the Tomodachi Game.

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:29.410
Onigawara Hyakutaro

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:29.410
Hashiratani Chisato

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:29.410
Kadokura Juzo

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:29.410
Niwa Banri

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:29.410
Shinomiya Kei

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:29.410
It tests friendships.

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:32.960
In other words, it's not simply that 
we have a better chance

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:35.730
of finding their hider because we have more people?

00:13:35.730 --> 00:13:38.120
That isn't the strategy?

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:40.750
Correct. Think carefully.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:43.640
What did Manabu explain 
about the game rules?

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:49.560
From here on, you will all play 
hide-and-seek in this vast forest.

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:54.350
Where exactly does this vast forest 
begin, and how far does it go?

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:56.120
Huh?! How far?

00:13:56.120 --> 00:13:59.070
It does look like a really huge forest.

00:13:59.070 --> 00:14:01.610
Whether you had two or
 four people searching,

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:04.280
it would be nearly impossible 
to find someone.

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:05.650
Exactly.

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:10.010
You've got to realize that since 
he used the vague words "vast forest,"

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:14.410
the game isn't about blindly
searching for someone who's hiding.

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:17.740
How do you find the other team's hider, then?

00:14:17.740 --> 00:14:19.420
The important point is...

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:24.510
The searchers have to 
bring food to the hiders.

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:31.220
Hider

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:28.260
The rule that searchers have
 to carry food to the hiders,

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:31.220
because the hiders can't move.

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:31.220
Seeker

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:32.910
Oh, I get it.

00:14:32.910 --> 00:14:34.030
Huh...

00:14:34.030 --> 00:14:35.500
I've solved all of the mysteries.

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:36.930
Huh? Huh?!

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:39.730
Hyakutaro, you seriously still don't get it?

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:41.940
Huh?! No way!

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:44.420
But Captain, if we're doing that,

00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:46.470
The hell?! Of course I get it!

00:14:44.420 --> 00:14:47.540
shouldn't we put someone 
at the food station right away?

00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:48.870
Yes, we should.

00:14:48.870 --> 00:14:53.340
Oh, but I'm one of the slowest runners here.

00:14:53.340 --> 00:14:56.080
In that case, Hyakutaro and Chisato,

00:14:56.540 --> 00:15:01.130
you two have the fastest legs on the team, 
so go ahead to where the food is.

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:02.500
Y-Yes, sir!

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:03.760
Roger.

00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:07.550
Kei and Banri, go find 
a hiding place for me.

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:09.250
You have good eyes for that sort of thing,

00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:12.070
so I'm sure you'll pick 
somewhere I won't be found.

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:17.710
All right! Before we get going, 
let's do the usual thing!

00:15:17.710 --> 00:15:19.970
Huh? Are we really going to do it here?

00:15:19.970 --> 00:15:22.650
Shut it, Chisato. C'mon and huddle.

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:27.300
Right, here we go.

00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:28.530
One, two—

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:29.400
<b>Fast Fight</b>

00:15:28.970 --> 00:15:32.350
Fast fight! Swift win! 
Solid walls! Strong team!

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:30.280
<b>Swift Win</b>

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:31.150
<b>Solid Walls</b>

00:15:31.400 --> 00:15:32.030
<b>Strong Team</b>

00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:32.910
<b>We Are</b>

00:15:32.350 --> 00:15:34.520
We are! The best!

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:33.950
<b>The Best</b>

00:15:37.930 --> 00:15:40.620
Victory!

00:15:41.340 --> 00:15:43.250
Well, did you see that?

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:45.660
Their team has perfect unity.

00:15:46.030 --> 00:15:49.470
After two games, they're totally in sync

00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:52.590
thanks to the guidance 
of their genius leader.

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:55.340
I'll admit their unity is impressive.

00:15:56.090 --> 00:15:57.360
It's kind of gross, though.

00:15:57.360 --> 00:15:58.100
Huh?!

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:03.890
But instead of five typical friends, 
they're more like a single team.

00:16:03.890 --> 00:16:05.350
That's right!

00:16:05.350 --> 00:16:10.560
They're all members of the same 
sports club. They're teammates.

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:15.490
Some of them were childhood friends, 
but they're all different ages

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:18.250
and have a rigid age-based hierarchy.

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:22.350
That's exactly why you could
 say that they're linked

00:16:22.350 --> 00:16:26.580
by the strong bonds of discipline and order, 
moreso than any equal friendship.

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:28.660
Bonds, huh?

00:16:28.660 --> 00:16:31.550
W-What? That isn't to your liking?

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:34.880
Fine. Here's your advance warning.

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:37.730
This game will be over in three days.

00:16:37.730 --> 00:16:40.820
And, of course, my Group K 
will be the victors.

00:16:41.380 --> 00:16:44.500
I know because they've truly figured out

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:46.980
a perfect strategy for winning.

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:51.640
And it's one that only the five 
members of Group K can use.

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:55.990
<b>Third Game: Day 3</b>

00:16:53.050 --> 00:16:55.990
It's the third day. You said you'd win.

00:16:56.330 --> 00:16:58.470
You really think the winner 
will be decided today?

00:16:58.470 --> 00:17:00.060
Of course.

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:05.110
<i>Take a look at Mikasa Tenji 
and that expression on his face.</i>

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:08.250
<i>He's bound to press the give-up button.</i>

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:12.100
<i>The strategy for Friendly 
Hide-and-Seek is extremely simple.</i>

00:17:12.100 --> 00:17:15.580
<i>When the hider can't stand 
the thirst and hunger anymore,</i>

00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:17.570
<i>and a searcher goes to take him food,</i>

00:17:17.570 --> 00:17:19.850
<i>the other team just has to follow.</i>

00:17:20.630 --> 00:17:22.860
<i>Just like they were saying in Group K,</i>

00:17:22.860 --> 00:17:26.940
<i>it would be next to impossible 
to find someone hiding in this forest.</i>

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:31.050
<i>When someone gets lost, 
even if they want to be rescued,</i>

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:35.440
<i>even with many more people searching, 
it's still very difficult to find them.</i>

00:17:35.440 --> 00:17:40.500
<i>The trick is to always be in a position 
to tail the other team,</i>

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:44.160
<i>and then to make sure they 
don't lose you when you do.</i>

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:48.600
<i>Group K won't have any trouble with that.</i>

00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:51.530
<i>First of all, they have 
four people to watch two.</i>

00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:54.320
<i>If they work in shifts, they'll
be ready to follow at any time.</i>

00:17:54.320 --> 00:17:57.100
<i>Second, they're athletes 
and really tight teammates.</i>

00:17:57.100 --> 00:18:01.010
<i>The other two won't be able to 
run fast enough to get away.</i>

00:18:01.010 --> 00:18:05.100
<i>Basically, if Group C moves 
right now, they'll be tailed,</i>

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:07.240
<i>and their hider will be spotted.</i>

00:18:07.240 --> 00:18:09.790
<i>Their defeat is a matter of course.</i>

00:18:09.790 --> 00:18:11.540
<i>And if they don't move,</i>

00:18:11.540 --> 00:18:14.190
<i>the hider will eventually succumb 
to hunger and thirst</i>

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:15.600
<i>and push the give-up button.</i>

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:19.780
<b>Third Game</b>

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:19.780
<b>Group C  Friendly Hide-or-Seek</b>

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:19.780
<b>Defeated</b>

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:20.480
<i>Either way, they're bound to lose.</i>

00:18:20.480 --> 00:18:22.450
<i>And it's impossible the other way around.</i>

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:25.200
<i>Even if only three from 
Group K go to deliver food,</i>

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:27.490
<i>the other two won't be able to follow.</i>

00:18:27.490 --> 00:18:30.740
<i>Also, compared to someone 
who's been eating properly,</i>

00:18:30.740 --> 00:18:34.420
<i>a person who hasn't eaten for three days 
has a massive handicap to begin with.</i>

00:18:35.770 --> 00:18:39.680
<i>By my estimate, he'll reach 
his breaking point tonight.</i>

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:44.300
<i>Either they lose when 
Katagiri Yuichi is followed,</i>

00:18:44.300 --> 00:18:46.660
<i>or they lose when Mikasa Tenji gives up.</i>

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:48.030
<i>It's a matter of time.</i>

00:19:10.780 --> 00:19:12.790
Sorry to keep you waiting, Tenji.

00:19:13.520 --> 00:19:16.840
Y-Yuichi...

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:21.340
Thanks, Tenji. I'm glad 
you trusted me and waited.

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:25.820
Of course I did. I said I'd trust you.

00:19:28.180 --> 00:19:32.940
W-What's this? What is happening?

00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:36.260
Who in the world is he talking to?

00:19:36.920 --> 00:19:41.200
He's probably hallucinating 
due to extreme stress and hunger.

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:44.490
He's envisioning the thing 
he most wants to see.

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:45.830
How dreadful.

00:19:46.360 --> 00:19:50.410
Even if it is hopeless, you'd 
think his teammate could at least

00:19:50.410 --> 00:19:52.750
search for the other hider 
or call to cheer him up.

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:56.190
But to do absolutely nothing like this...

00:19:57.030 --> 00:20:00.810
For two days, this jerk hasn't 
left the food station at all

00:20:00.810 --> 00:20:02.340
and has just been eating and sleeping.

00:20:02.710 --> 00:20:07.100
He's also been blabbing all sorts of info 
about his team to the other side.

00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:11.800
Does he really intend to
abandon Mikasa Tenji after all?

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:16.230
Hey, is Maria just going to sit 
there silently the whole time?

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:19.480
She might just be an observer for now,

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:22.810
but she <i>is </i>still supposed to act 
as a member of Group C, right?

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:27.010
Yes, but she did send me just one report.

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:33.120
"Katagiri Yuichi is even more of a crazy 
asshole than I thought," she said.

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:38.840
It seems he's started something 
while we've been talking.

00:20:39.220 --> 00:20:43.140
Hey guys, I have a request 
to make of Group K.

00:20:46.330 --> 00:20:49.850
I want to switch to Group K.

00:20:53.800 --> 00:21:00.480
Yuichi, this rice ball... looks delicious...

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:05.910
<i>Katagiri Yuichi... This guy really is...</i>

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:10.120
<i>the worst.</i>

00:21:08.570 --> 00:21:10.330
<b>The Worst</b>

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:15.640
Perhaps Katagiri Yuichi is a true 
supporter of gender equality,

00:21:15.640 --> 00:21:20.420
given that he's equally merciless in the way
 he uses both males and females like tools.

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:23.920
<b>NEXT: Hurry Up and "Switch Sides"</b>
